  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Taiwanese Hokkien narrative song in which a singer half-chants long rhymed tales from kua-a songbooks to a small stock of tunes, self-accompanied on the long-necked Taiwanese moon lute (gueh-khim), often with a partner on the daguangxian fiddle; liam-koa was already on Taiwanese 78 rpm records in the 1930s (the yueqin card stands in for the gueh-khim).",
